From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:18:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gpio: apple-d2365: refuse sleep when the wake mask write
 fails

apple_pmic_gpio_suspend() warned and went on when writing the event wake
mask failed. The system then slept with wake sources the PMIC would not
report, and could not be woken by them. Return the error so that the
suspend is aborted, and drop the IRQ lock on that path.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpio/gpio-apple-d2365.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpio/gpio-apple-d2365.c b/drivers/gpio/gpio-apple-d2365.c
index ba66e8eab..c516dfe30 100644
--- a/drivers/gpio/gpio-apple-d2365.c
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpio-apple-d2365.c
@@ -588,8 +588,10 @@ static int apple_pmic_gpio_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	mutex_lock(&gpio->irq_lock);
 	/* Only wake-enabled events may pull the line while asleep. */
 	ret = apple_pmic_event_sync(gpio, gpio->wake);
-	if (ret)
-		dev_warn(dev, "event wake mask write failed: %d\n", ret);
+	if (ret) {
+		mutex_unlock(&gpio->irq_lock);
+		return ret;
+	}
 	gpio->suspended = true;
 	mutex_unlock(&gpio->irq_lock);
 	/* A thread that passed the gate before it closed has finished now. */
